From: beyond2lte camera enablement <noreply@localhost>
Date: 2026-11-23
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: add a CameraSensorHelper for the Samsung S5K3P9

The software ISP AGC needs a CameraSensorHelper to convert between analogue
gain and the sensor's gain register code. Without one, the softisp IPA only
logs "Failed to create camera sensor helper" and AGC drives gain as a raw
code, so exposure control is wrong.

The S5K3P9 (beyond2lte rear ultra-wide) analogue gain register (0x0204) is
linear: code = 32 * gain, i.e. code 32 = 1.0x, 512 = 16.0x. In the
CameraSensorHelper linear model gain = (m0*x + c0)/(m1*x + c1) with x the
register code, that is { m0=1, c0=0, m1=0, c1=32 }.

Black level is 64 at 10 bits = 4096 on libcamera's 16-bit scale (64 << 6),
the same value the datasheet-derived imx219 helper uses.

Without this patch the camera still enumerates and previews; gain tracking is
just coarse. It is therefore optional for the first milestone but recommended.

Signed-off-by: beyond2lte camera enablement <noreply@localhost>
---
 src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -552,6 +552,18 @@
 	}
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("imx219", CameraSensorHelperImx219)
+
+class CameraSensorHelperS5k3p9 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperS5k3p9()
+	{
+		/* Black level 64 at 10 bits; analogue gain code = 32 * gain. */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 32 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("s5k3p9", CameraSensorHelperS5k3p9)
 
 class CameraSensorHelperImx258 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
